From 8b8ab7a755145bfae6f4690dea7b8f7f9197c8f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:22:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/112] Song: loading an audio track no longer writes
 Instrument::existsOnCard into it

Song::readFromFile() set ((Instrument*)newOutput)->existsOnCard = true for every output it loaded, audio tracks
included. An AudioOutput is no Instrument: the cast wrote a 1 into byte 0x61 of it, which is inside its
GlobalEffectableForClip part. In v17 that was a byte of some effect member (harmless enough to go unseen); once that
part is 8-byte aligned (at 0x60, v18's EQ state has 64-bit members) it is the part's vtable pointer, and the first
render of an audio track jumped to nowhere (tests/song, the emulator). Now only instruments get the flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/model/song/song.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/model/song/song.cpp b/src/deluge/model/song/song.cpp
index 9662adfd..bf1e25db 100644
--- a/src/deluge/model/song/song.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/model/song/song.cpp
@@ -1952,7 +1952,12 @@ loadOutput:
 						if (error != Error::NONE) {
 							goto gotError;
 						}
-						((Instrument*)newOutput)->existsOnCard = true;
+						// (Only an Instrument has existsOnCard: for an audio track (AudioOutput, no Instrument) the
+						// cast wrote a 1 into byte 0x61 of it, inside its GlobalEffectableForClip part: mastertune v18,
+						// whose EQ state made that part 8-byte aligned at 0x60, had its vtable pointer broken there)
+						if (newOutput->type != OutputType::AUDIO) {
+							((Instrument*)newOutput)->existsOnCard = true;
+						}
 						*lastPointer = newOutput;
 						lastPointer = &newOutput->next;
 					}
